      "id": "5ud4g8s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Measurement of Temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Temperature decreases with altitude in the troposphere at the Normal Lapse Rate of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters.",
        "Horizontal temperature distribution is governed by latitude, altitude, distance from the sea, ocean currents, air masses, and local topography.",
        "Temperature inversion is an atmospheric phenomenon where warm air overlays cold air near the surface, reversing the normal vertical profile.",
        "Isotherms bend more sharply in the Northern Hemisphere due to higher land-water contrast compared to the ocean-dominated Southern Hemisphere.",
        "The Urban Heat Island (UHI) effect leads to elevated ambient temperatures in dense urban centers relative to surrounding rural zones."
      ],
      "id": "guq78px"
    },
